15. FIRST VERSION OF HUMOUR RANKING

For each candidate, score internally on dimensions such as:
- relevance
- specificity
- surprise
- voice match
- medium fit
- personal recognition
- novelty
- edge fit
- topical fit
- clarity
- likely cringe
- policy/platform risk

Do not expose all of these as fake precision to users.
Use them internally to compare candidates.

Start with model-as-judge + explicit user selection.
Replace/adapt weights as real behaviour accumulates.


16. WHAT NOT TO BUILD YET

Do not build:
- giant general Etsy analytics graph
- broad marketplace engine
- custom foundational humour model
- elaborate RL stack before enough feedback
- dozens of product categories
- avatar technology from scratch
- own print infrastructure
- full Moonpig competitor
- generic =E2=80=9CAI gift generator=E2=80=9D

Use existing frontier models for:
- image generation
- video/avatar generation
- speech
- writing
- multimodal understanding

Swap providers as quality/cost changes.

Own:
- humour framework
- templates
- evaluation
- ranking
- taste adaptation
- feedback loop
- brand identity
- user experience


17. SAFETY / TRUST / PRIVACY

Personal humour can become creepy if the system surfaces private
information unexpectedly.

Rules:
- ask before using broader Muse history/context for a gift
- pass a minimised context summary to humour tooling
- provide =E2=80=9Cmild / savage / topical / no personal history=E2=80=9D c=
ontrols
- allow avoid-topics
- avoid sensitive personal attributes by default
- do not expose private facts to a recipient merely because Muse knows them
- do not treat harmful/offensive output as automatically =E2=80=9Cfunnier=
=E2=80=9D
- keep marketplace/IP rules distinct from creative edge

The brand can be rude, dry, absurd, edgy and politically incorrect
without making =E2=80=9Charm=E2=80=9D the objective.


