22. SUCCESS CRITERIA

Roast.pet MVP is =E2=80=9Cdone=E2=80=9D when:
- a user can upload a pet photo
- provide or permit enough context
- receive 3 genuinely distinct joke concepts
- the system selects a suitable visual format
- one concept becomes a good-looking print-ready card
- user can buy/send it without manual design work
- interaction events are captured for learning

Humour Module v1 is =E2=80=9Cdone=E2=80=9D when:
- another app can call it without Roast.pet-specific logic
- it can select between multiple humour structures
- it adapts tone to profile/context
- it can format for at least card + social
- evaluation fixtures catch regressions

FunnyLabs v1 is =E2=80=9Cdone=E2=80=9D when:
- every generated/tested joke carries structured metadata
- outcomes can be joined back to templates/profiles
- top-performing structures can be identified
- updates can improve ranking without rewriting the whole app


23. NORTH STAR

The north star is not:
=E2=80=9Cmake funny AI cards.=E2=80=9D

It is:

=E2=80=9Cmake agents actually funny.=E2=80=9D

Roast.pet is the first commercial wedge because pets + personalised
gifting + cards create a narrow, understandable, emotionally
compelling product.

FunnyLabs is the learning system.

The Humour Module is the reusable infrastructure.

Muse gives it personal context.

Commerce connectors turn the result into atoms.

Social stand-up gives it a high-volume experimental arena.

If the system works, it can eventually power:
- personalised cards
- personalised gifts
- social avatars
- AI companions
- brand agents
- synthetic comedians
- creator tools
- entertainment agents
- humour evaluation APIs

The long-run asset is a continuously improving understanding of which
comedic structures, tones and formats work for which contexts and
audiences =E2=80=94 without depending on any single LLM, avatar model,
marketplace or fulfilment provider.

ONE-LINE VERSION

FunnyLabs learns what humans actually find funny; the Humour Module
packages that learning for agents; Roast.pet proves it by turning
personal context and a pet into genuinely funny personalised gifts
through Muse and existing commerce/fulfilment rails.
